# Example 1616: Repeated fresh() appends in an ordinal domain
# Regression test: appending after the maximum many times along one path
# must keep working. fresh() allocates the midpoint between the current
# maximum and the top of the ID range, so each append halves the space
# left above the maximum. The model checker respaces the stored ordinal
# IDs by rank before that space runs out.
# Demonstrates: ordinal fresh(), ordinal ID respacing

# Only one timestamp is live at a time, so the limit never binds. Every
# state is distinct (count differs), so symmetry reduction cannot merge
# the path: all 100 appends run back to back.

TIMES = symmetry.ordinal(name="ts", limit=2)

action Init:
    t = TIMES.fresh()
    count = 0

atomic fair action Append:
    require count < 100
    t = TIMES.fresh()
    count += 1

always eventually assertion ReachesHundred:
    return count == 100
